From a3b41d29c7a1039c49ca9ac2f5f236de6c6e3f55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: max rossi <113717219+maxr0ssi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:05:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] d3dx9: Run preshader instructions through direct register
 pointers.

Preshaders are re-executed on BeginPass() and CommitChanges() whenever one of
their inputs was set, and every component of every instruction went through
exec_get_arg() (relative addressing and wrap checks), regstore_get_double()
(a switch on the table type), a function pointer and regstore_set_double().
RotWK's vertex shader preshaders (defaultw3d.fxo) are ~70 instructions reading
camera, light, fog, material and per-object parameters, and the game re-sets
those for every batch and the per-object ones for every mesh: interpreting them
was ~70 % of the effect framework's main-thread time.

Once the register tables exist, give every instruction whose operands are
directly addressed float or double registers pointers to them, and run it in a
loop with the common operations inlined. The same registers are read and
written in the same order (inputs of component j, then component j) and every
result comes from the same double precision operation, so the results are bit
identical. Instructions with relative addressing, other register types or too
many arguments keep the generic path.

WINE_D3DX9_FXOPT is a bit mask of these effect shortcuts (default: all); clear
0x1 to turn this one off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
